 own)",[657,809,810],{},"—",[636,812,813,820,825,833],{},[657,814,815],{},[397,816,818],{"href":817},"\u002Fcomponents\u002Fchoice\u002Fradio-group",[309,819,359],{},[657,821,822],{},[309,823,824],{},"URadioGroup",[657,826,827,312,830,807],{},[309,828,829],{},"legend",[309,831,832],{},"item-append",[657,834,810],{},[636,836,837,844,849,855],{},[657,838,839],{},[397,840,842],{"href":841},"\u002Fcomponents\u002Fchoice\u002Fcheckbox-group",[309,843,356],{},[657,845,846],{},[309,847,848],{},"UCheckboxGroup",[657,850,851,312,853,807],{},[309,852,829],{},[309,854,832],{},[657,856,810],{},[636,858,859,866,871,876],{},[657,860,861],{},[397,862,864],{"href":863},"\u002Fcomponents\u002Fchoice\u002Fswitch",[309,865,362],{},[657,867,868],{},[309,869,870],{},"USwitch",[657,872,873],{},[309,874,875],{},"label",[657,877,810],{},[879,880,881,888,921,934,948],"ul",{},[882,883,884,885,328],"li",{},"Inherited props are only used for type inference; at runtime they are passed to the underlying component through ",[309,886,887],{},"$attrs",[882,889,890,891,894,895,312,897,312,899,312,901,903,904,907,908,911,912,914,915,917,918,920],{},"Props the component handles itself are not inherited and do not show up in autocompletion, such as ",[309,892,893],{},"modelValue",". Input-style components (",[309,896,341],{},[309,898,344],{},[309,900,365],{},[309,902,368],{},") show their own loading icon, always using Nuxt UI's ",[309,905,906],{},"appConfig.ui.icons.loading",", so ",[309,909,910],{},"loadingIcon"," is excluded as well and has no effect. ",[309,913,347],{}," lets ",[309,916,776],{}," show the loading icon, so ",[309,919,910],{}," works as usual.",[882,922,923,924,926,927,930,931,328],{},"Events are forwarded to the underlying component through ",[309,925,887],{}," as usual, with types taken from the underlying component's emits; for example, the argument of ",[309,928,929],{},"@blur"," is a ",[309,932,933],{},"FocusEvent",[882,935,936,937,940,941,943,944,947],{},"Checkboxes, switches and groups support descriptions (",[309,938,939],{},"description","; for groups, the item's ",[309,942,939],{}," field or the field set by ",[309,945,946],{},"descriptionKey","): without a description the height matches an input of the same size; with one, the item grows and the description wraps, while its first line still lines up with fields without a description. The label stays on one line and is truncated with a tooltip showing the full text.",[882,949,950,951,954,955,578,958,960,961,963,964,966],{},"Checkboxes and groups do not support Nuxt UI's ",[309,952,953],{},"variant"," (card, table), ",[309,956,957],{},"indicator",[309,959,468],{},": the border and padding of card and table make options taller; ",[309,962,957],{}," moves the checkbox, while the loading spinner stays where the left checkbox is; ",[309,965,468],{}," only changes the border color of card and table. Passing them is a type error and they are not applied at runtime.",[479,968,970],{"id":969},"slots","Slots",[305,972,973,974,316,977,980,981,983,984,986,987,316,990,993],{},"Input-style components can use ",[309,975,976],{},"#leading",[309,978,979],{},"#trailing"," to put icons or buttons before and after the input; ",[309,982,347],{}," can use every slot of ",[309,985,776],{},". Checkboxes and groups have their own ",[309,988,989],{},"#append",[309,991,992],{},"#item-append"," for content next to the option label.",[330,995],{"name":996},"common-slots",[879,998,999,1007],{},[882,1000,1001,1002,388,1004,1006],{},"The ",[309,1003,979],{},[309,1005,344],{}," sits next to the unit and the loading icon without replacing them.",[882,1008,1009,1010,328],{},"See the component pages for the slot props, for example ",[397,1011,1013],{"href":1012},"\u002Fcomponents\u002Fchoice\u002Fradio-group#item-append-content","Item append content",[479,1015,650],{"id":1016},"exposed-refs",[305,1018,1019],{},"After getting the component with a template ref, use the refs in the table to work with the underlying native elements, for example to focus, select all or open the menu.",[330,1021],{"name":1022},"common-expose",[300,1024,1025],{"id":319},"Skeleton",[305,1027,1028,1029,1031],{},"The skeleton keeps the layout space of the original control, following ",[309,1030,382],{},", width, textarea rows and the option group layout, with no fixed height of its own. While it is on, the component cannot be clicked or used with the keyboard, and tooltips and open menus close.",[305,1033,1034],{},"A common use is an edit page loading data from the back end, with one loading state controlling the skeleton of every field. Press \"Reload data\" to try it: the layout stays the same during the skeleton, and the data fills in when it arrives.",[330,1036],{"name":1037},"common-skeleton",[305,1039,1040,1041,1043,1044,1046,1047,1049],{},"Compared with ",[309,1042,315],{},": ",[309,1045,315],{}," keeps the current value and shows a spinner inside the field, suited to a field doing its own work (such as fetching select options); ",[309,1048,319],{}," covers the whole field, suited to when the page data has not arrived yet and the current value means nothing.",[300,1051,1053],{"id":1052},"locales","Locales",[305,1055,1056,1057,1060,1061,578,1064,1067,1068,1071],{},"Component texts (placeholders, accessible names, validation messages, date picker texts and so on) follow the Nuxt UI locale (",[309,1058,1059],{},"\u003CUApp :locale>","), with Traditional Chinese and English built in; components already on screen update immediately when it changes. The default texts mentioned on these pages are the English ones. Text props passed explicitly (such as ",[309,1062,1063],{},"title",[309,1065,1066],{},"placeholder",") are not affected by the locale. See ",[397,1069,47],{"href":1070},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftheme\u002Fmessages"," for setup and overrides.",[305,1073,1074],{},"\"Component language\" in the palette menu at the top right of the docs site switches the language of the component examples on the page; by default it follows the docs language.",[300,1076,1078],{"id":1077},"empty-values","Empty values",[305,1080,1081,1082,1085,1086,1089,1090,312,1092,312,1094,312,1096,312,1098,316,1100,1102,1103,1106,1107,1110,1111,316,1113,1115],{},"When the parent binds ",[309,1083,1084],{},"null"," \u002F ",[309,1087,1088],{},"undefined",", the components below write back the agreed empty value; unexpected values such as wrong types are also cleared to the agreed empty value. This applies both on mount and when the parent fills values in later. When clearing an unexpected value, ",[309,1091,341],{},[309,1093,365],{},[309,1095,344],{},[309,1097,359],{},[309,1099,374],{},[309,1101,350],{}," log a ",[309,1104,1105],{},"console.warn"," (",[309,1108,1109],{},"[ShuoComponentName] … cleared","); ",[309,1112,347],{},[309,1114,371],{}," only clear, without a warning.",[630,1117,1118,1127],{},[633,1119,1120],{},[636,1121,1122,1124],{},[639,1123,641],{},[639,1125,1126],{},"Empty value",[652,1128,1129,1146,1164,1176],{},[636,1130,1131,1141],{},[657,1132,1133,312,1135,312,1137,312,1139],{},[309,1134,341],{},[309,1136,365],{},[309,1138,359],{},[309,1140,374],{},[657,1142,1143],{},[309,1144,1145],{},"''",[636,1147,1148,1152],{},[657,1149,1150],{},[309,1151,347],{},[657,1153,1154,1157,1158,1110,1160,1163],{},[309,1155,1156],{},"emptyValue"," (default ",[309,1159,1145],{},[309,1161,1162],{},"[]"," when multiple",[636,1165,1166,1172],{},[657,1167,1168,312,1170],{},[309,1169,344],{},[309,1171,371],{},[657,1173,1174],{},[309,1175,1084],{},[636,1177,1178,1182],{},[657,1179,1180],{},[309,1181,350],{},[657,1183,1184,1186,1187,1189],{},[309,1185,1145],{}," for a single date, ",[309,1188,1162],{}," for a range",[305,1191,1192,1193,1195,1196,1198,1199,328],{},"Press \"Apply null from the back end\" to simulate the back end returning ",[309,1194,1084],{}," for every field: the bound values below change to each component's agreed empty value. ",[309,1197,356],{}," does not write back and stays ",[309,1200,1084],{},[330,1202],{"name":1203},"common-empty-value",[305,1205,1206],{},"These components do not write back the parent's value:",[879,1208,1209,1218,1226],{},[882,1210,1211,1043,1213,1215,1216,328],{},[309,1212,356],{},[309,1214,1084],{}," or a non-array value shows everything unchecked; checking an option writes back the full array. Clearing gives ",[309,1217,1162],{},[882,1219,1220,1222,1223,328],{},[309,1221,353],{},": shows unchecked when the bound value is not ",[309,1224,1225],{},"trueValue",[882,1227,1228,1043,1230,1232],{},[309,1229,368],{},[309,1231,1084],{}," after clearing.",[1234,1235,1236],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sHwdD, html code.shiki .sHwdD{--shiki-light:#90A4AE;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-default:#546E7A;--shiki-default-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#676E95;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic}html pre.shiki code .sMK4o, html code.shiki .sMK4o{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF}html pre.shiki code .swJcz, html code.shiki .swJcz{--shiki-light:#E53935;--shiki-default:#F07178;--shiki-dark:#F07178}html pre.shiki code .spNyl, html code.shiki .spNyl{--shiki-light:#9C3EDA;--shiki-default:#C792EA;--shiki-dark:#C792EA}html pre.shiki code .sfazB, html code.shiki .sfazB{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#C3E88D;--shiki-dark:#C3E88D}html pre.shiki code .sTEyZ, html code.shiki .sTEyZ{--shiki-light:#90A4AE;--shiki-default:#EEFFFF;--shiki-dark:#BABED8}html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-defaul